2b:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Decision quality and system cost"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["A correct instruction can still fail during grasping or placement. We therefore keep ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"decision correctness"}],", checkpoint progress ",["$","$L1a",null,{"term":"P"}],", and full-task success ",["$","$L1a",null,{"term":"success"}]," separate. Extra perception and verification also carry a cost: REMM is not the fastest or most query-efficient system on every task, and successful recovery can keep a run active longer than an early baseline stop."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The following efficiencies are relative scores, not seconds or query counts. For each task and cost, the best observed median receives 100; other scores are 100 × best median / system median. Higher means lower cost."}]]}]
