2f:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Remembering is not the same as grounding"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["HiMe and REMM recall the demonstrated sequence similarly well. Their difference appears when that memory must ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"identify an object and produce the next instruction"}],". Destination recognition alone remains strongest for the no-memory baseline."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"On T3, the no-memory baseline always selects the middle cup and matches the fixed-set majority reference of 11/30. Uniform random selection is 33.3% in expectation. REMM’s 30/30 has a Wilson 95% interval of 88.6–100%; it does not establish perfect tracking under real-world occlusion or appearance changes."}]]}]
